                                    <div class="sidenav-content">
                                        <p class="LastUpdated">Last published: <span class="mc-variable Puppet.LastUpdated variable">November 19, 2026</span></p>
                                        <div role="main" id="mc-main-content">
                                            <h1 class="concepttitle" data-mc-autonum="" id="PE202601" data-magellan-target="PE202601"><span class="autonumber"><span></span></span><span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026.0.1</h1>
                                            <div>
                                                <p class="page-toc-intro" data-mc-autonum="On this page"><span class="autonumber"><span>On this page</span></span><b>:</b>
                                                </p>
                                                <ul data-magellan="" data-animation-duration="250" data-active-class="selected" data-scroll-container=".body-container" data-scroll-container-on="only screen and (min-width: 1280px)" class="nocontent menu _Skins_MenuProxy mc-component">
                                                    <li class="tree-node"><a href="#PE202601">PE 2026.0.1</a>
                                                        <ul>
                                                            <li class="tree-node"><a href="#PuppetEnterpriselifecycleupdate">Puppet Enterprise® lifecycle update</a>
                                                            </li>
                                                            <li class="tree-node"><a href="#Enhancements">Enhancements</a>
                                                            </li>
                                                            <li class="tree-node"><a href="#Platformsupport">Platform support</a>
                                                            </li>
                                                            <li class="tree-node"><a href="#Resolvedissues">Resolved issues</a>
                                                            </li>
                                                        </ul>
                                                    </li>
                                                </ul>
                                            </div>
                                            <p class="shortdesc">Released November 2026</p>
                                            <p class="shortdesc"><span class="mc-variable Puppet.PELong variable">Puppet Enterprise (PE)</span> 2026.0.1 delivers security, platform support, and reliability improvements, including stricter authorization rule matching, enhanced protection of <span class="mc-variable Puppet.Forge variable">Forge</span> authorization tokens, support for Oracle Linux 10 x86_64 agents, and improvements to cloud database, backup, and orchestration operations. This release also includes fixes for multiple security vulnerabilities.</p>
                                            <h2 data-mc-autonum="" id="PuppetEnterpriselifecycleupdate" data-magellan-target="PuppetEnterpriselifecycleupdate"><span class="autonumber"><span></span></span><span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEMedium variable">Puppet Enterprise</span><sup>®</sup> lifecycle update</h2>
                                            <p>Starting in August 2026, <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEMedium variable">Puppet Enterprise</span> transitioned its software support model from Long-Term Support (LTS) and Short-Term Support (STS) to the Latest and Latest-1 model. This change applies to both PE and PE Advanced. To learn more, see <a href="https://www.puppet.com/products/puppet-enterprise/support-lifecycle"><span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEMedium variable">Puppet Enterprise</span> Platform Support Lifecycle</a>.</p>
                                            <div class="important">
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li>
                                                        <p>Puppet Enterprise (PE) 2026 is our leading-edge PE release stream (also referred to as Latest).</p>
                                                    </li>
                                                    <li>
                                                        <p>For important information about upgrading to <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026, see <a href="upgrading_pe.htm">Upgrade Puppet Enterprise</a>.</p>
                                                    </li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li>
                                                        <p>If you're on <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2025, your release series is designated Latest-1 and continues to receive security updates, defect fixes, and technical support. Release notes and other information are available in the <a href="https://help.puppet.com/pe/2025.11/topics/puppet-enterprise.htm"><span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2025 documentation.</a></p>
                                                    </li>
                                                </ul>
                                                <ul>
                                                    <li>
                                                        <p>If you're on <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2023.8, the final release series under <span class="mc-variable Puppet.ProductName variable">Puppet Enterprise</span>'s legacy Long-Term Support (LTS) model,  you're currently in the overlap support period, which ends on February 27, 2027. You'll find release notes and other information in the <a href="https://help.puppet.com/pe/2023.8/topics/puppet-enterprise.htm">2023.8 documentation</a>.</p>
                                                    </li>
                                                    <li>
                                                        <p>Customers running releases that have reached end of maintenance and support (EOMS) are encouraged to upgrade to a currently supported <span class="mc-variable Puppet.ProductName variable">Puppet Enterprise</span> release.</p>
                                                    </li>
                                                </ul>
                                            </div>
                                            <div class="note">To access the release notes for the Puppet<sup>®</sup> platform, including Puppet agent, Puppet Server, Facter, and PuppetDB, see <a href="https://www.puppet.com/docs/puppet/8/release_notes_osp">Platform release notes</a>.</div>
                                            <h2 class="sectiontitle" data-mc-autonum="" id="Enhancements" data-magellan-target="Enhancements"><span class="autonumber"><span></span></span>Enhancements</h2>
                                            <p><b>Authorization rules now use stricter certificate name matching</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>Authorization rules in <code>auth.conf </code>now match certificate names more strictly. Rules that specify a hostname match only certificates with that exact name. Wildcard rules such as <code>*.example.com</code> now match only names under <code>example.com</code> and no longer match <code>example.com</code> itself. If you rely on a wildcard rule to allow the bare domain, add a separate rule for that domain name.</p>
                                            <h2 class="sectiontitle" data-mc-autonum="" id="Platformsupport" data-magellan-target="Platformsupport"><span class="autonumber"><span></span></span>Platform support</h2>
                                            <p><b>Agent platforms added</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>This release adds support for the <span class="mc-variable Puppet.Puppet variable">Puppet</span> agent on the following operating system platforms:</p>
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>
                                                    <p>Oracle Linux 10 x86_64</p>
                                                </li>
                                            </ul>
                                            <h2 class="sectiontitle" data-mc-autonum="" id="Resolvedissues" data-magellan-target="Resolvedissues"><span class="autonumber"><span></span></span>Resolved issues</h2>
                                            <p><b>Cloud database installs no longer grant CONNECT access to PUBLIC</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>In <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2025.12.0 and 2026.0, cloud database deployments could leave <code>CONNECT</code> privileges granted to <code>PUBLIC</code> on most <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> databases. This allowed other roles on the same database instance to establish connections to those databases. <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> now revokes <code>CONNECT</code> access from <code>PUBLIC</code> for cloud database deployments, aligning cloud database behavior with local installations. This issue is resolved in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2025.12.1 and 2026.0.1. <b>[PE-47115]</b></p>
                                            <p style="font-weight: bold;">Database connection permissions now converge correctly on migrated Cloud SQL deployments</p>
                                            <p>In <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2025.12.0 and 2026.0, <span class="mc-variable Puppet.Puppet variable">Puppet</span> runs on deployments migrated from local PostgreSQL to Google Cloud SQL could repeatedly report changes because database connection permissions were not applied correctly for some <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> databases. As a result, the deployment might never reach a converged state. This issue is resolved in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2025.12.1 and 2026.0.1. <b>[PE-47136]</b></p>
                                            <p><b>pe-bolt-server now validates upload file paths</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>In previous releases, the <code>pe-bolt-server</code> upload file handler did not sufficiently validate file paths supplied in upload requests. <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> now validates upload paths to ensure uploaded files remain within the intended job cache directory. This issue is resolved in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2025.12.1 and 2026.0.1. <b>[PE-47314]</b></p>
                                            <p><b>Daily log rotation no longer interrupts running plans</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>In previous <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> versions, daily log rotation could restart the <code>pe-plan-runner</code> service while a plan was running. This caused orchestrated plans to abort before completion and could affect infrastructure workflows such as replica upgrades. This issue is resolved in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026.0.1, 2025.12.1 and 2023.8.13 <b>[PE-47319]</b></p>
                                            <p><b>Certificate-only restores no longer cause CA inconsistencies on database-backed deployments</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>In <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026.0 and 2025.12.0, using <code>puppet-backup restore --scope=certs</code> on a primary configured to use the database CA backend could leave the restored CA files out of sync with the CA data stored in the pe-ca database. As a result, SSL communication and configuration operations could fail. This issue is resolved in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026.0.1 and 2025.12.1 <b>[PE-47558]</b></p>
                                            <p><b>CD4PE jobs no longer fail with <span class="mc-variable Puppet.Puppet variable">Puppet</span> agent 9.1.1</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>In <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026.0.0, <code>cd4pe_jobs</code> module version 1.7.5 could fail when running jobs with <span class="mc-variable Puppet.Puppet variable">Puppet</span> agent 9.1.1 due to a missing dependency. As a result, repository and script payloads could fail to decompress, causing job execution to fail with an <code>uninitialized constant GZipHelper::FileUtils</code> error. This issue is resolved in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026.0.1, 2025.12.1 and 2023.8.13. <b>[PE-47501]</b></p>
                                            <p><b>Updated trust stores remove revoked certificate authorities</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p><span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> now includes updated certificate trust stores that remove the compromised eMudhra intermediate CA certificates from the bundled trust chain. In addition, <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> components that use the Go runtime have been updated to incorporate the latest certificate validation protections. These changes are included in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026.0.1, 2025.12.1, and 2023.8.13. <b>[PE-47591]</b></p>
                                            <p><b>Backups now work with password-authenticated external PostgreSQL databases</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>In <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2025.12.0 and 2026.0, <code>puppet-backup create</code> could fail on installations that use an external PostgreSQL server with password authentication (<code>puppet_enterprise::database_cert_auth: false</code>). Database passwords were no longer available through <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PuppetDB variable">PuppetDB</span>, causing backup operations that include databases to fail authentication. <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> now retrieves database credentials from a secure local source, allowing backups to complete successfully on affected installations. This issue is resolved in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span>   2026.0.1 and 2025.12.1. <b>[PE-47131]</b></p>
                                            <p><b>Code Manager </b><span style="font-weight: bold;" class="mc-variable Puppet.Forge variable">Forge</span><b> authorization tokens are now protected</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>In previous releases, a Code Manager <span class="mc-variable Puppet.Forge variable">Forge</span> authorization token could be exposed in agent output, reports, and <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PuppetDB variable">PuppetDB</span>. <span class="mc-variable Puppet.ProductName variable">Puppet Enterprise</span> now handles <span class="mc-variable Puppet.Forge variable">Forge</span> authorization tokens as sensitive values, preventing them from being displayed in these locations. In addition, the <code>/etc/puppetlabs/r10k/r10k.yaml</code> file is no longer world-readable by default. This issue is resolved in <span class="mc-variable Puppet.PEShort variable">PE</span> 2026.0.1, 2025.12.1, and 2023.8.13. <b>[PE-47972]</b></p>
                                            <p><b>Security fixes</b>
                                            </p>
                                            <p>The following CVEs were fixed in PE:</p>
